      "text": "## What \"Strange\" and \"Attractor\" Each Mean"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md#006",
      "path": [
        "06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:dynamical-systems:06-strange-attractors, git-history:dynamical-systems:06-strange-attractors]",
        "canonical_path": "dynamical-systems/06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md",
        "concepts": "[strange, attractors]",
        "current_path": "dynamical-systems/06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md",
        "id": "maxim:dynamical-systems:strange-attractors",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "dynamical-systems",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[strange, attractors]",
        "section": "dynamical-systems",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Strange Attractors",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "```\n   ATTRACTOR (the dynamics):                STRANGE (the geometry):\n   - invariant: flow maps it to itself      - FRACTAL: non-integer dimension\n   - attracting: a neighborhood (basin)       (Lorenz dim ~ 2.06: more than a\n     of initial conditions converges to it     surface, less than a volume)\n   - minimal: no smaller attractor inside   - infinitely layered \"millefeuille\"\n                                              sheet structure (Cantor-like\n   Three classical NON-strange attractors:    cross-section)\n     fixed point (dim 0)\n     limit cycle (dim 1)        STRANGE  = fractal geometry + chaotic dynamics\n     torus (dim 2, quasi-per.)   (the two almost always coincide, but the\n                                  words name different things)\n```"
    },
    {
      "id": "06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md#007",
      "path": [
        "06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:dynamical-systems:06-strange-attractors, git-history:dynamical-systems:06-strange-attractors]",
        "canonical_path": "dynamical-systems/06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md",
        "concepts": "[strange, attractors]",
        "current_path": "dynamical-systems/06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md",
        "id": "maxim:dynamical-systems:strange-attractors",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "dynamical-systems",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[strange, attractors]",
        "section": "dynamical-systems",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Strange Attractors",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "> **Operational definition.** A set `A` is a strange attractor if it is (1) an attractor — invariant,\n> with an open basin draining onto it, and minimal — and (2) the dynamics on it have a **positive\n> largest Lyapunov exponent** (chaos). Its fractal dimension follows from the Lyapunov spectrum via\n> the Kaplan–Yorke formula (below)."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md#008",
      "path": [
        "06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md"
      ],
      "level": 0,
      "line": 1,
      "metadata": {
        "backsource_ids": "[mdloom-backfill:dynamical-systems:06-strange-attractors, git-history:dynamical-systems:06-strange-attractors]",
        "canonical_path": "dynamical-systems/06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md",
        "concepts": "[strange, attractors]",
        "current_path": "dynamical-systems/06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md",
        "id": "maxim:dynamical-systems:strange-attractors",
        "index_roles": "[guide, root-concept]",
        "kind": "guide",
        "maxim_schema": "maxim.frontmatter.v1",
        "module": "dynamical-systems",
        "remap_from": "[]",
        "remap_to": "[]",
        "root_concepts": "[strange, attractors]",
        "section": "dynamical-systems",
        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Strange Attractors",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The defining tension: **dissipation contracts volume to zero, chaos forbids collapse to a point.**\nThe only geometric resolution is a set of *zero volume but positive (fractional) dimension* — a\nfractal. Strange attractors are what that contradiction forces into existence."
    },
    {
      "id": "06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md#009",
      "path": [
        "06-STRANGE-ATTRACTORS.md"
      ],
