        "source_custody": "partial",
        "status": "source-custody",
        "title": "Strange Attractors",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "| You already know | Strange-attractor framing |\n|---|---|\n| A stable equilibrium / setpoint a controller drives to | The attractor for that loop; a strange attractor is the chaotic generalization |\n| Steady-state vs transient response | Transient = approach through the basin; steady state = motion *on* the attractor |\n| State-space trajectory of a plant | The attractor is the long-term invariant set in that same state space (`control-theory/02`) |\n| Rayleigh–Bénard convection rolls | Lorenz is a 3-mode truncation of exactly that PDE — `fluid-dynamics/` |\n| Reconstructing a signal's state from samples | Takens embedding: rebuild the attractor from one scalar time series |"
    },
